From fb188859764149d92bf72a88180c097c1c207ec4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 19:07:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] remove every figure the data does not support, and every
 control that lied
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A full audit of all eight pages. Findings are measured against the shipped
client/public/data.json (1,298 projects, 18,172 review rows, 15,646 of
them carrying a status), not inspected by eye.

FABRICATED CONTENT REMOVED
--------------------------
- Dashboard "+23 seit letzter Woche" under the live project count. There
  is no time series in the data — no created-at, no snapshot, nothing to
  difference — so the number could only ever have been typed in.
- Dashboard "Datenbank: Online" and "Excel Sync: Aktiv", each with a
  pulsing green dot. Both false for the reason the third indicator in the
  same card was already removed: production is a static SPA, there is no
  database connection and no sync process. Nothing polled them.
- Login "Version 1.0.0" against package.json 2.0.0 — the same drift
  Footer.tsx documents as fixed by reading the Vite define.
- Wizard "22 Fragen" in two places; Step 2 renders 19 in Projektanmeldung
  and 18 in Projektkonfiguration. Now derived from the mode.
- Step 3's frozen "18.172 Prüfzeilen" in a component with no data in
  scope, and its promise that mail "folgt in Stufe 4".
- Step 5's "PDF-Export ... folgt in Stufe 4", printed on a screen that
  already renders a working "Checkliste als PDF" button.

CHARTS THAT DROPPED ROWS
------------------------
- The "Alle Gewerke" pie was five hardcoded buckets matched by exact
  string: it plotted 14,587 of 15,646 rows and silently dropped 1,059 —
  Projektkonfig. 474, Prüfung erfolgt 229, Niederschrift erstellt 180 +
  80 annotated, zurückgestellt 44, Projektkonfiguration 33, prüffähig 19.
  All 260 sign-offs were missing from a chart headed "alle". It also
  painted Nachforderung red where status-appearance.ts gives it amber.
  Now grouped by tone: 8 slices, 8 distinct colours, every row counted,
  and the tooltip names the statuses folded into each. Per-status slices
  would have been complete but unreadable — 12 statuses share 8 tones, so
  four pairs would have had one colour and one legend swatch.
- Per-Gewerk pies keyed on the raw status, so statusHex fell through to
  its neutral grey: TBQ's 80 "Niederschrift erstellt (LP05-05-01-F31)"
  rows rendered in exactly the grey used for 688 "nicht erforderlich" —
  a completed sign-off painted as irrelevant. Verbatim the regression
  status-appearance.ts exists to prevent.
- Recharts matched <Cell> to slice by index while the Pie got a filtered
  array: every colour would have shifted the moment a bucket hit zero.
- Truncated lists now say so: "Status pro Gewerke — 8 von 14" and
  "Regionale Verteilung — Top 5 von 8". They were hiding 6 departments
  and 288 projects under headings that claimed coverage.

COUNTS THAT WERE WRONG
----------------------
- "Projekte mit Verzögerung" compared r.status to two literals, a third
  definition of "open" on a page that already had two. It missed
  Nachforderung and prüffähig and every annotated variant: 304 shown,
  347 real. The date also went through new Date(), which reads a
  date-only string as UTC midnight and shifts a day west of Greenwich.
- The reviewer roster was a hardcoded list of 37. It missed 8 of the 44
  reviewers in the data — 985 rows, Haberla 512, Colak 250, Wagner 83 —
  so Colak, third by volume, never appeared in "Top Performer" at all.
  It also listed "Zentrale" twice: a duplicate React key, and its
  workload double-counted. Derived from the data now.
- "Niederschrift erstellt (LP05-...)" never counted as completed in the
  workload panel.
- The activity timeline keyed on date+project+status, which is not
  unique: one reviewer signing two Gewerke on the same project on the
  same day collapsed onto one key and React dropped 1,509 rows. The
  department is now in the key and on screen.
- KPI caption read "Abgelehnt / Nachforderung" over a value that counts
  only abgelehnt and gestoppt — 122 shown, 204 described.
- Two different numbers were both labelled "Prüfzeilen" on one screen.

CONTROLS THAT LIED
------------------
- The header search box, present on every route, searched nothing: no
  submit, no navigation, no callback out of the component. It now hands
  the term to /projects?q=, which also makes a result set linkable.
- The map's onBoundsChange fed four parameters that useProjects declares
  and never reads, so every pan and zoom re-rendered the page and changed
  nothing while the count still said 1.298. Wiring removed rather than
  left looking functional.
- The notification bell read a localStorage key nothing writes:
  useNotifications() is imported nowhere, so the store was always empty.
  It now shows the audit trail — the app's only real event stream.
- The avatar had cursor-pointer and a hover ring with no menu behind it.
- 72 of the 138 populated projektLink values are free-text notes, not
  URLs; three places rendered them as anchors, producing a relative href
  that opens the app's own 404. One rule now, in shared/project-link.ts.

BVB-EEA AND PSV-ITK
-------------------
Never reviewed until now, and 105 near-identical lines each, so every
defect existed twice. Collapsed into one DepartmentReviewTable:
- raw status into statusBadgeClass — 3 ITK rows mis-coloured today
- new Date().toLocaleDateString() — drops the leading zero (627 of 757
  dated EEA rows disagree with the detail dialog) and shifts a whole day
  west of Greenwich
- 8 `any` at an already-typed boundary
- a sticky thead in a container with no height, so with 814 unpaginated
  rows the column labels left the screen and never came back
- one spinner for loading, empty AND failed alike
- "Verwaltung der EEA-Freigabeerklärungen" on a page with no controls,
  listing 231 rows that are explicitly not Freigaben
- "Datum" on a Projektvorstellungen page showing the Prüfdatum: the two
  differ on 355 of 510 rows
- three columns with whitespace-nowrap, so a 96-character Station in one
  row set the width for all 814 — the table measured 2,499px against a
  1,066px viewport, now 1,268px

ACCESSIBILITY
-------------
- The review-status <select> was the only unlabeled control in the app,
  and it writes.
- Both suggestion lists used onMouseDown, which never fires from Enter or
  Space: mouse-only.
- The sidebar resize handle was a <div> with onMouseDown, unusable by
  keyboard and by touch. Now role="separator", focusable, arrow keys,
  pointer events.
- Nav items exposed no aria-current; the filter panel no aria-expanded;
  the 14 department toggles no aria-pressed.
- The fullscreen map had no Escape.
- Dashboard rendered nothing for loading or failure, so a failed read
  produced a confident dashboard of zeros.

REGRESSION FIXED FROM MY OWN LAST PATCH
---------------------------------------
The coarse-pointer ::after hit area applied to both buttons in the table's
action cell — two 44px strips 32px apart overlap by 12px and the later
sibling wins hit-testing, so on touch, tapping the right edge of "Details
anzeigen" opened the Kommentar dialog. The strip is now scoped to cells
with a single control; the two-button cell gets real 44px targets in a
flex row. Forcing width alone made them wrap and tripled the row to 97px.

Seven new e2e assertions pin all of it, including one that reads the pie
caption and compares it against a row count computed independently from
data.json.

Gates: 0 type errors · 145 passed / 6 skipped · 72 lint warnings (down
from 80: -8 noExplicitAny, -4 noForEach) · e2e 35/35 · responsive 61/61 ·
map chrome 6/6.
